{
  "id": "andritz_spl_diversity_v2",
  "description": "Redundancy-heavy queries where the corpus indexes the same manual under many projects. Diversity is gated by expected_distinct_content (distinct CONTENT documents after stripping the project/archive filename prefix, via _content_key), NOT expected_distinct_documents — the latter counts per-project copies of one manual as distinct and is therefore vacuous on this corpus (kept at 0 here; distinct_documents is still reported for diagnostics). Thresholds calibrated on live measurements (2026-06-15, balanced profile): single-manual queries (g150 operating instructions, LH2 0113) expect 1; queries where the corpus genuinely offers 3+ distinct relevant manuals expect 3. Baseline (MMR on) passes 7/10: div_002 and div_006 surface only 2 distinct contents (real diversity shortfall), div_008 misses its expected source. An A/B MMR on/off shows no pass-rate gap and near-identical per-case distinct_content (round-robin keys on document_id, MMR on embeddings — neither separates per-project copies meaningfully here).",
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "div_001_g150_operating_instructions_multiproject",
      "query": "Where can I find the G150 speed controller operating instructions?",
      "collection": "andritz-notices-techniques-spl-pilot",
      "expected_sources": [
        "g150 operating instructions"
      ],
      "expected_evidence_terms": [
        "G150",
        "operating instructions"
      ],
      "expected_intent": "source_lookup",
      "forbidden_route": "catalogue_inventory",
      "latency_profile": "balanced",
      "language": "en",
      "expected_distinct_documents": 0,
      "expected_distinct_content": 1
    },
    {
